{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The first of your grain.</b> This is terumah, and Scripture did not specify a measure for it, but our Sages gave it a measure: a generous eye — one out of forty; a grudging eye — one out of sixty; average — one out of fifty. And they relied on Scripture not to give less than one out of sixty, as it says (Ezekiel 45) ״a sixth of an ephah from a homer of wheat״ — a sixth of an ephah is half a se'ah; when you give half a se'ah per kor, that is one out of sixty, for a kor is thirty se'in (Jerusalem Talmud, Trumot 4)." "<b>And the first of the fleece of your sheep.</b> When you shear your flock each year, give from it the first portion to the priest. And Scripture did not specify a measure for it, and our Sages gave it a measure — one out of sixty. And how many sheep are obligated in the first of the fleece? Five ewes, as it says (I Samuel 25) ״וחמש צאן עשויות.״ Rabbi Akiva says: ״ראשית גז״ — two; ״צאנך״ — four; ״תתן לו״ — that makes five (see Sifrei and Hullin 135)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:34.607980737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}